From 4d91b800a90224b40f23c88161e983cd7a31ab64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vedaant <vedaant12345@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:51:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): forward model discovery on named compat mounts

GET /compat/<name>/v1/models returned 404 cave_route_not_found because
adapter routes are an inference-only (POST) allowlist, so clients could
not refresh their model catalog through the proxy.

Add a dedicated GET route on the mux. It authenticates first, selects the
adapter exactly as the inference route would, maps credentials and headers
through the adapter, keeps the caller's User-Agent and query verbatim, and
relays the upstream status, headers and body unchanged under a bounded
timeout. It reads no body and never inspects, compresses, captures or
records, so discovery does not touch token accounting.

Only named mounts serve discovery; the default /compat/ adapter would turn
any unnamed segment into an upstream path. HEAD, POST and every other
method keep their existing proxy-route behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 proxy/internal/gateway/compat_models.go      | 102 ++++++++
 proxy/internal/gateway/compat_models_test.go | 262 +++++++++++++++++++
 proxy/internal/gateway/server.go             |   3 +
 3 files changed, 367 insertions(+)
